        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>3B81.4 Splenosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63044,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> autotransplanted splenic tissue</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63045,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63046,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "<p>Abdomen and/or pelvis {28543860}</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-19T16:09:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63047,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Splenosis is usually an incidental finding, although it can occasionally produce pelvic pain, intestinal obstruction, bleeding, etc. {28543860; 21867352} or can be mistaken for endometriosis or malignancy {21867352; 29651643}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63048,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Splenosis is uncommon in women {29651643} and is typically seen in patients ranging in age from 29 to 60&nbsp;years {30931139; 28543860; 23809236}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63049,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It results from the disruption of the spleen due to trauma, splenectomy, or spontaneous rupture due to haematological or infectious processes {21867352}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63050,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Splenosis is caused by direct seeding of splenic tissue or haematogenous spread {21867352}. The interval between the causative incident and the diagnosis of splenosis ranges from a few months to &gt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;years {21867352; 30363257}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63051,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Splenosis presents as dark-red to bluish, solitary or multiple lesions ranging from a few millimetres to &gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;cm, although lesions &gt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;cm are rare {28543860; 26076145; 29651643}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63052,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tissue may mimic normal spleen or show a distorted architecture {28543860}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63053,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 161,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:08:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
